_refine.details                                  
;NO ELECTRON DENSITY WAS OBSERVED FOR THE N-TERMINAL RESIDUE
ALA 30 AND FOR RESIDUES ASP 450  - THR 460. PRESUMABLY THEY
ARE DISORDERED.  THESE RESIDUES ARE PART OF A FLEXIBLE
LINKAGE BETWEEN CATALYTIC CORE AND C-TERMINAL HEMOPEXIN
PARTS OF MMP-2.

RESIDUES 108 - 116 WERE MODELED INTO POOR ELECTRON DENSITY.
THE SIDE CHAIN ORIENTATIONS WERE TAKEN FROM THE ROTAMER
LIBRARY.  THESE RESIDUES ARE IN THE LOOP WHICH CONECTS
PROPEPTIDE AND CATALYTIC DOMAIN.

THE ELECTRON DENSITY FOR THE SURFACE LOOP 649 - 652 IS
WEAK, AND THE INDIVIDUAL B-FACTORS ARE RATHER HIGH.
;
